<title>SINGAPORE: SIA declines comment on Ansett/SIA report.</title>
<headline>SIA declines comment on Ansett/SIA report.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines (SIA) declined to comment on Tuesday on a report that it is in preliminary talks to become an equal partner with News Corp Ltd and Air New Zealand Ltd (Air NZ) in regional operator Ansett Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>An SIA spokesman told Reuters he could not comment on the report.</p>
<p>The Australian Financial Review had reported the talks and said SIA could pay between Australian $200 million A$300 million to buy a one-third stake.  </p>
<p>SIA in April did confirm it had had talks with Ansett and Air NZ over a &quot;commercial relationship&quot;, but gave no details.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
